<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds sailed higher into the close on Thursday in the wake of a buoyant Bund market and ahead of a public holiday in Spain on Friday.</p>
<p>Dealers said the domestic market had offered little support for bonos. The Bank of Spain left its key money market rate unchanged at 5.25 percent as expected earlier in the session.</p>
<p>&quot;We remain linked to Germany while trying to keep the (10-year) spread steady,&quot; said one analyst. &quot;We are still trading without domestic influence as we do not expect the Bank of Spain to lower rates before the end of the summer.&quot;</p>
</text>
